{"id":"3b8ae1e2-c14d-44f8-8325-e21580c59eb6","expr":"opcode != 255","rationale":"Opcode 255 is not a recognized JVM opcode.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.cglib.transform.MethodVisitorTee#visitInsn(int):void","file":"org/springframework/cglib/transform/MethodVisitorTee.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:39.376793654Z"}
{"id":"116e6775-ab4c-46f0-b8a6-c79852c0b1ef","expr":"opcode != -1","rationale":"Opcode values are non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.cglib.transform.MethodVisitorTee#visitInsn(int):void","file":"org/springframework/cglib/transform/MethodVisitorTee.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:39.376793654Z"}
{"id":"16d6c9a6-bb7f-4ef4-8321-962566cae4e9","expr":"opcode >= 0","rationale":"The opcode likely represents a bytecode instruction, which is usually a non-negative integer.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.cglib.transform.MethodVisitorTee#visitInsn(int):void","file":"org/springframework/cglib/transform/MethodVisitorTee.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:39.377027155Z"}
{"id":"5b5a2962-8ca3-4ae1-a1f3-9ecf32b18440","expr":"opcode <= 255","rationale":"In Java bytecode, opcode is an unsigned byte value between 0 and 255.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.cglib.transform.MethodVisitorTee#visitInsn(int):void","file":"org/springframework/cglib/transform/MethodVisitorTee.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:39.377027155Z"}
{"id":"c5b89c81-e8cf-4abe-87b6-8047a4a36a57","expr":"opcode >= 0","rationale":"Opcode represents bytecode instructions which are usually non-negative integers.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.cglib.transform.MethodVisitorTee#visitIntInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/cglib/transform/MethodVisitorTee.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:39.385116808Z"}
{"id":"1a0b7f8a-068b-4ead-8510-0a386a79f631","expr":"operand >= 0","rationale":"Operand in visitIntInsn likely to be non-negative as it represents an integer operand.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.cglib.transform.MethodVisitorTee#visitIntInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/cglib/transform/MethodVisitorTee.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:39.385116808Z"}
{"id":"5c2bdceb-b4fa-4bcf-979f-6d711e3a2972","expr":"(opcode == 16) || (opcode == 17) || (opcode == 18) || (opcode == 19) || (opcode == 20)","rationale":"visitIntInsn is called only for certain opcodes within the JVM which typically include BIPUSH (16), SIPUSH (17), etc.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.cglib.transform.MethodVisitorTee#visitIntInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/cglib/transform/MethodVisitorTee.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:39.385116808Z"}
