{"id":"84d78770-107c-4e36-8513-33492492185f","expr":"(opcode != 169) || var >= 0","rationale":"For the RET opcode (169), the var must be a valid non-negative local variable index.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.cglib.transform.MethodVisitorTee#visitVarInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/cglib/transform/MethodVisitorTee.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:39.392460825Z"}
{"id":"8723a13d-bc42-4a56-a864-6f5179473f40","expr":"opcode != 0","rationale":"visitVarInsn should only be called with opcodes corresponding to variable instructions, which are not zero.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.cglib.transform.MethodVisitorTee#visitVarInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/cglib/transform/MethodVisitorTee.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:39.392460825Z"}
{"id":"f1d63411-09f3-46a2-86bd-f59a6788429c","expr":"var < 65536","rationale":"The var index is limited by JVM to a maximum of 65535 as these are usually represented with unsigned short.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.cglib.transform.MethodVisitorTee#visitVarInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/cglib/transform/MethodVisitorTee.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:39.392460825Z"}
