{"id":"6f095157-805a-4fe7-822d-7ec95e5c0566","expr":"numStack >= 0","rationale":"Number of stack items cannot be negative.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFrame(int,int,Object[],int,Object[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:43.860245747Z"}
{"id":"a2d6bdaf-c346-4638-9939-abda4b66f066","expr":"(local == null && numLocal == 0) || (local != null && local.length >= numLocal)","rationale":"If local array exists, it must have length at least numLocal; if null, then numLocal must be zero.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFrame(int,int,Object[],int,Object[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:43.860245747Z"}
{"id":"0281eb3c-aa19-4b8a-b7d1-3704a3fcc531","expr":"(stack == null && numStack == 0) || (stack != null && stack.length >= numStack)","rationale":"If stack array exists, it must have length at least numStack; if null, then numStack must be zero.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFrame(int,int,Object[],int,Object[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:43.860245747Z"}
{"id":"9366fb49-0d9d-40b1-a3e4-b703c35783f8","expr":"type == 0 || type == 1 || type == 2 || type == 3 || type == 4 || type == 5","rationale":"The frame type must be one of the predefined constants (e.g., Opcodes.F_NEW, F_FULL, etc.).","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFrame(int,int,Object[],int,Object[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:43.860245747Z"}
{"id":"ef83ecf4-540e-488e-a564-7880656a6f2c","expr":"opcode >= 0","rationale":"Opcodes in ASM are typically non-negative integers corresponding to opcode values.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInsn(int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:43.868282618Z"}
{"id":"fcc60c2b-29b1-4f45-8763-9c8344888527","expr":"opcode < 256","rationale":"ASM opcodes fit within a byte, so they must be less than 256.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInsn(int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:43.868282618Z"}
{"id":"72c88b32-ccc8-4ec9-8366-e7e4c453c794","expr":"opcode >= 0 && opcode <= 255","rationale":"Opcode values are expected within the unsigned byte range, consistent with standard JVM opcode ranges.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInsn(int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:43.917089488Z"}
{"id":"7032cff6-c18b-461e-b7ad-6ac66895a7c2","expr":"operand >= -32768 && operand <= 65535","rationale":"Operand is likely constrained to fit in 16-bit range for these instructions.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitIntInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:43.924786289Z"}
{"id":"842ec0f0-c303-4238-8b9c-a94601edaa5a","expr":"varIndex >= 0","rationale":"Local variable indices are non-negative indices.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitVarInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:43.927282048Z"}
{"id":"3732278f-eb53-4b0a-bed8-036b36b074cf","expr":"opcode >= 0","rationale":"Opcode should be non-negative as valid instruction codes.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitVarInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:43.927282048Z"}
{"id":"183554fd-3215-4d07-a1e2-073565982f58","expr":"varIndex < 256 || varIndex >= 256","rationale":"Either varIndex is below 256 or at least 256 to choose encoding path.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitVarInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:43.927282048Z"}
{"id":"055a1bb9-42bb-44c7-918a-9c5159ba32ea","expr":"opcode >= 0","rationale":"Opcode values represent instruction codes, typically non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitVarInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:43.927354665Z"}
{"id":"a784f16a-6e81-4402-8be1-45a6d66e64d1","expr":"varIndex >= 0","rationale":"Variable indexes in bytecode are always zero or positive.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitVarInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:43.927354665Z"}
{"id":"505bb934-d18d-470a-b953-3b54c0fc8588","expr":"type != null","rationale":"The type parameter is used by symbolTable.addConstantClass(type), which requires type to be non-null","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTypeInsn(int,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:43.934896825Z"}
{"id":"b084f368-b7e4-4685-92f1-8e32630838e5","expr":"opcode >= 0","rationale":"Opcodes represent instruction codes and are usually non-negative integers","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTypeInsn(int,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:43.934896825Z"}
{"id":"ce1da8a9-8e2f-45fd-a5fc-0af3f93ad336","expr":"opcode <= 255","rationale":"Java bytecodes opcodes are defined as 1-byte unsigned values, so their values are between 0 and 255 inclusive","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTypeInsn(int,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:43.934896825Z"}
{"id":"2e7d5abd-4b89-4890-8317-768803af2d7a","expr":"!type.isEmpty()","rationale":"The type string represents a class name and should not be empty","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTypeInsn(int,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:43.934896825Z"}
{"id":"756528b4-4e77-4610-94c0-9bb90c0c1a62","expr":"owner != null","rationale":"The internal name of the class owning the field should be a valid (non-null) string.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFieldInsn(int,String,String,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:43.988873939Z"}
{"id":"793c548e-7972-4942-af8a-29f8ae8dfdc9","expr":"name != null","rationale":"The name of the field should be non-null as a valid identifier.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFieldInsn(int,String,String,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:43.988873939Z"}
{"id":"80a6062e-9730-40cd-a9c2-53c3c1ff5fc3","expr":"descriptor != null","rationale":"The field descriptor is mandatory and must be non-null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFieldInsn(int,String,String,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:43.988873939Z"}
{"id":"9ab45dfa-de49-43fe-8b5c-12e487b3e437","expr":"opcode >= 0 && opcode <= 255","rationale":"Opcodes in the JVM bytecode are in the range 0 to 255 (byte values).","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFieldInsn(int,String,String,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:43.988873939Z"}
{"id":"81a8c344-f73a-48a0-a668-1b1605379097","expr":"(opcode == 178 || opcode == 179 || opcode == 180 || opcode == 181)","rationale":"The method deals with field instructions, so opcode must be one of the four related opcodes.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFieldInsn(int,String,String,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:43.988873939Z"}
{"id":"40bb96e1-3c5b-480d-ac96-9dd2ff330715","expr":"(opcode == 185) == isInterface","rationale":"If the opcode indicates an interface method invocation, the isInterface boolean should be true, otherwise false.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitMethodInsn(int,String,String,String,boolean):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:43.991786453Z"}
{"id":"22ee5f42-1985-49a4-978a-afbedad973b0","expr":"owner != null","rationale":"The owner of the method invoked should be a valid class name string and should not be null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitMethodInsn(int,String,String,String,boolean):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:43.991786453Z"}
{"id":"feb9d2b2-2eb2-4d99-aa8a-c48020d74957","expr":"name != null && name.length() > 0","rationale":"The method name must be a valid non-empty string to represent the invoked method.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitMethodInsn(int,String,String,String,boolean):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:43.991786453Z"}
{"id":"f30749a3-6dd8-48da-9465-1bc44ae0f652","expr":"descriptor != null && descriptor.length() > 0","rationale":"Method descriptor is expected to be valid non-empty string describing the method signature.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitMethodInsn(int,String,String,String,boolean):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:43.991786453Z"}
{"id":"2297ecee-6e92-452b-a368-e8d1ec5f08f5","expr":"opcode != 0","rationale":"Opcode should be a valid JVM instruction opcode and is unlikely to be zero at this point in the code.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitMethodInsn(int,String,String,String,boolean):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:43.991786453Z"}
{"id":"cb9da7cd-0dff-4fd5-baf8-143cb850e6f2","expr":"owner != null","rationale":"The owner parameter is the internal name of the method's owner class and must not be null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitMethodInsn(int,String,String,String,boolean):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:43.992899008Z"}
{"id":"0f878f0b-c972-462a-b2e5-d4f6e7fb0d94","expr":"name != null","rationale":"The method name identifies the method and should always be non-null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitMethodInsn(int,String,String,String,boolean):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:43.992899008Z"}
{"id":"1f2c74b5-5f62-46bf-ac85-2075e3c34b72","expr":"descriptor != null","rationale":"The method descriptor describes the types of arguments and return value and hence must be non-null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitMethodInsn(int,String,String,String,boolean):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:43.992899008Z"}
{"id":"9d875dbf-d52d-48d5-adbc-7ae96c7fc3ac","expr":"opcode >= 0","rationale":"The opcode parameter represents a JVM bytecode instruction and is expected to be non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitMethodInsn(int,String,String,String,boolean):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:43.992899008Z"}
{"id":"5ed9799f-0350-4690-a01c-3fdb83c9043e","expr":"opcode == 178 || opcode == 179 || opcode == 180 || opcode == 181","rationale":"The opcode corresponds to one of the GETSTATIC, PUTSTATIC, GETFIELD, or PUTFIELD instructions.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFieldInsn(int,String,String,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:43.993139861Z"}
{"id":"379c04f1-3d57-4134-a322-e526530839ec","expr":"owner != null && name != null && descriptor != null","rationale":"The method requires non-null owner, name, and descriptor strings to add fieldref symbol.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFieldInsn(int,String,String,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:43.993139861Z"}
{"id":"07baed1b-6580-43da-a6c5-34512465ce44","expr":"(opcode == 178 || opcode == 179) || (opcode == 180 || opcode == 181)","rationale":"The opcode partitions into static (GETSTATIC, PUTSTATIC) and instance (GETFIELD, PUTFIELD) field instructions.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFieldInsn(int,String,String,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:43.993139861Z"}
{"id":"96af2105-5be6-4e59-8aff-1bb81a13ab30","expr":"opcode >= 0 && opcode <= 255","rationale":"The opcode parameter corresponds to JVM opcode values which are typically in the range 0 to 255.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTypeInsn(int,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:43.995934583Z"}
{"id":"dd03747f-a04f-45b0-872e-2f8e90ccc58f","expr":"type != null && !type.isEmpty()","rationale":"The type argument, representing a class/type descriptor, should be a valid non-null non-empty string.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTypeInsn(int,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:43.995934583Z"}
{"id":"24b5e677-3fd9-435d-8c28-13b848c4935f","expr":"!type.contains(\" \")","rationale":"The internal name provided by 'type' is expected to be a valid descriptor without spaces.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTypeInsn(int,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:43.995934583Z"}
{"id":"87f1f1ba-898a-4f15-ba3a-d99f4d3e73b2","expr":"name != null","rationale":"The name parameter should represent a method or field name and thus must be non-null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInvokeDynamicInsn(String,String,Handle,Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.003429193Z"}
{"id":"85260f05-e57e-4def-a968-0dc0d424fafc","expr":"descriptor != null","rationale":"The descriptor defines the method type descriptor and must always be present.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInvokeDynamicInsn(String,String,Handle,Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.003429193Z"}
{"id":"3418f2d5-5e0b-40f2-a5cc-b675f6614ac0","expr":"bootstrapMethodHandle != null","rationale":"The bootstrap method handle is essential for resolving the invoke dynamic call site.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInvokeDynamicInsn(String,String,Handle,Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.003429193Z"}
{"id":"117a4ca2-d88e-4f81-a6a8-33c152e2260f","expr":"bootstrapMethodArguments == null || bootstrapMethodArguments.getClass().isArray()","rationale":"Bootstrap method arguments represent varargs and are modeled as Object, so they must be an array type or null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInvokeDynamicInsn(String,String,Handle,Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.003429193Z"}
{"id":"3d33a0a3-f92e-4336-b12e-6caf91cf36b0","expr":"opcode >= 0","rationale":"Opcode values are generally non-negative integers representing bytecode instructions","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitJumpInsn(int,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.071032322Z"}
{"id":"81d9508a-29c7-4ac2-866f-88dcd59497e6","expr":"name != null","rationale":"The name of the method or dynamic call must be non-null for the invoke dynamic instruction to be valid.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInvokeDynamicInsn(String,String,Handle,Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.074369184Z"}
{"id":"45de46f9-68c7-4548-a8aa-75f0f5573947","expr":"label != null","rationale":"The label parameter must be non-null because label.flags and label.put are accessed without null checks.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitJumpInsn(int,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.074606531Z"}
{"id":"08d22e58-95ee-45f7-903d-b1a1c52f9f22","expr":"label.flags >= 0","rationale":"Label flags are used in bitwise operations which are typically non-negative flags.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitJumpInsn(int,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.074606531Z"}
{"id":"31ab39fa-a6ac-4287-84b9-bcd8958ffeed","expr":"label != null","rationale":"The label parameter should never be null as it represents the label to be visited.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLabel(Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.074498387Z"}
{"id":"c6803cbd-69b3-4b77-9dfc-8a5071d66e09","expr":"label.flags >= 0","rationale":"Flags usually represent bit flags, so negative values don't make sense.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLabel(Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.074498387Z"}
{"id":"fb0f6d19-6bbc-4691-ba4e-6d5a9b0d94ed","expr":"label.bytecodeOffset >= 0","rationale":"Labels represent a position in bytecode, which is never negative.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLabel(Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.074498387Z"}
{"id":"cce8210b-f817-47fd-b8ee-915341e51187","expr":"opcode >= 0 && opcode <= 255","rationale":"In JVM bytecode, opcodes are between 0 and 255 inclusive.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitJumpInsn(int,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.074606531Z"}
{"id":"d611910c-7083-48b1-b64f-12e0214a8317","expr":"descriptor != null","rationale":"Because the method descriptor is fundamental to the bytecode instruction, it should not be null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInvokeDynamicInsn(String,String,Handle,Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.074369184Z"}
{"id":"74aa4885-d9aa-4d6a-8b75-e542607971b5","expr":"bootstrapMethodHandle != null","rationale":"This handle is necessary to create the constant invoke dynamic symbol.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInvokeDynamicInsn(String,String,Handle,Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.074369184Z"}
{"id":"4767c719-bcd7-4463-8653-d213df18e0e3","expr":"bootstrapMethodArguments == null || bootstrapMethodArguments.length >= 0","rationale":"Array length properties are always non-negative but this confirms non-null or empty args are possible.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInvokeDynamicInsn(String,String,Handle,Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.074369184Z"}
{"id":"62869695-3739-4fe5-812d-3e40bd3dc7b5","expr":"label.frame == null || label.frame.owner == label","rationale":"From the context, label.frame is either null or has owner field pointing to label; this maintains frame ownership consistency.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLabel(Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.074498387Z"}
{"id":"896432c6-608d-4d1e-baa1-9424f7e1bf0d","expr":"value != null","rationale":"The value passed to visitLdcInsn is typically a constant to be added; expecting non-null is common though null may be allowed.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLdcInsn(Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.089060223Z"}
{"id":"c170d16e-ddbb-48b6-bcae-237210a54a7c","expr":"label != null","rationale":"Label must be non-null at method exit.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLabel(Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.100225965Z"}
{"id":"c3ea64ea-138b-4557-bc48-40f66d41d1c4","expr":"label.frame == null || label.frame.owner == label","rationale":"The frame owner is updated to label or label.frame can be null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLabel(Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.100225965Z"}
{"id":"fa8259df-cb7a-4441-81c2-510f4469310e","expr":"label.bytecodeOffset >= 0","rationale":"Basic blocks and labels alignment imply non-negative bytecode offset.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLabel(Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.100225965Z"}
{"id":"e78f5a91-dcf1-4269-a865-1a3093346071","expr":"value != null || value == null","rationale":"value parameter may be null or non-null based on user input or caller context.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLdcInsn(Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.135776408Z"}
{"id":"cbd53d39-f6b7-4ec9-a1ae-c5caed6719ae","expr":"value == null || value.getClass() != null","rationale":"If value is non-null, calling getClass() is safe and returns non-null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLdcInsn(Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.135776408Z"}
{"id":"105e5f53-8477-4a05-a535-4196c20ef745","expr":"value == null || value.toString().length() >= 0","rationale":"Ensures that for non-null value, calling toString and length is safe and well-defined.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLdcInsn(Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.135776408Z"}
{"id":"8cd80f45-9f23-41d9-afcb-87e0175530e9","expr":"(varIndex >= 0)","rationale":"Local variable index should be non-negative as it refers to a variable slot in the frame.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.138836980Z"}
{"id":"0481934e-a212-4973-8ac1-4be0e9b426fc","expr":"(increment >= -128 && increment <= 127) || (varIndex > 255)","rationale":"If varIndex > 255 or increment is out of the range [-128, 127], the WIDE instruction is used.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.138836980Z"}
{"id":"f1fb29d8-6a90-49ea-bd62-a834d3eb64cf","expr":"varIndex < 256 || increment < -128 || increment > 127","rationale":"If varIndex is below or equal 255 and increment fits in signed byte, WIDE not used.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.138836980Z"}
{"id":"025d5b10-ef54-477e-a821-e00e76791f3b","expr":"increment >= -128 && increment <= 127","rationale":"Increment value for IINC must fit in signed byte if WIDE prefix is not used.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.138836980Z"}
{"id":"b956cfaf-7f28-4dc2-9fdd-ae9c0098813c","expr":"varIndex + 1 >= 1","rationale":"maxLocals is updated if current varIndex + 1 is greater than existing maxLocals, thus varIndex + 1 >= 1.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.138836980Z"}
{"id":"a918f279-3c95-4228-8926-2ed8734c0ff6","expr":"min <= max","rationale":"In a tableswitch instruction, the min bytecode value is always less than or equal to max to define a valid switch case range.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.141933229Z"}
{"id":"9dcb270b-a6e3-425d-a3eb-2636a24420d8","expr":"labels != null","rationale":"The labels parameter cannot be null because the method iterates over labels to put them to the code.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.141933229Z"}
{"id":"962ae79e-7980-49ba-9dac-85494c8321ab","expr":"varIndex >= 0","rationale":"Local variable indexes in bytecode are non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.141996328Z"}
{"id":"cfededd3-17f8-41f1-8cbe-5281b339b64d","expr":"increment <= 127","rationale":"Increment values fit in a signed byte range for the non-wide case.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.141996328Z"}
{"id":"85dc1901-5eb5-4173-840e-c08ac99c806a","expr":"labels.length == max - min + 1","rationale":"The label array should contain exactly one Label entry per possible switch value between min and max.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.141933229Z"}
{"id":"661465f7-defa-45fc-9b27-e658ab130b92","expr":"dflt != null","rationale":"The default label is used for all keys not covered by the range and labels, so it must be non-null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.141933229Z"}
{"id":"c097937a-2b9d-41e6-8067-f6167320eb9f","expr":"increment >= -128","rationale":"Increment values fit in a signed byte range for the non-wide case.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.141996328Z"}
{"id":"4230250b-4832-4d98-b620-e5f6d8ff21fb","expr":"(varIndex > 255) || (increment > 127) || (increment < -128)","rationale":"The method uses the WIDE instruction if any of these conditions is true.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.141996328Z"}
{"id":"f5a1feda-6d8f-431c-9d25-63929f6a95cd","expr":"varIndex <= 65535","rationale":"VarIndex when wide encoded must fit in a short according to standard JVM constraints.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.141996328Z"}
{"id":"116c3678-61d0-4906-836a-573a172f3da1","expr":"labels != null","rationale":"The labels array is documented as a varargs parameter and used in a loop and method calls, so it cannot be null here.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.155792713Z"}
{"id":"d92ba5c6-bc5f-4507-b885-245adb56a5f8","expr":"labels.length == max - min + 1","rationale":"A table switch requires a label for each value from min to max inclusive, so labels length equals max-min+1.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.155792713Z"}
{"id":"dae5e84b-284e-4105-add1-405090d3fff7","expr":"min <= max","rationale":"A table switch instruction requires a valid range with min <= max to be meaningful.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.155792713Z"}
{"id":"8ed11fdc-d55c-4c56-90aa-d9b0d7a143cb","expr":"dflt != null","rationale":"Since dflt.put() is called, dflt cannot be null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.155792713Z"}
{"id":"827ef91f-b2d2-42e1-ae7f-a4fa5244b8d2","expr":"labels.length >= 0","rationale":"Though trivial, this asserts labels array length is not negative.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.155792713Z"}
{"id":"ee8ae402-bd97-49a9-990a-daa41b84ca71","expr":"dflt != null","rationale":"A lookup switch instruction must have a valid default label.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.179092180Z"}
{"id":"7fe03900-2cac-4c3c-a7f8-836b991fc5c1","expr":"keys != null && labels != null","rationale":"The keys and labels arrays are essential for the lookup switch and cannot be null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.179092180Z"}
{"id":"2a9d469b-32c5-44ef-9e64-06fc37f14026","expr":"keys.length == labels.length","rationale":"Each key has a corresponding label, so the lengths must match.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.179092180Z"}
{"id":"f71cc4bd-b414-4b25-a4df-65ced1d70b7d","expr":"labels.length >= 0","rationale":"Array length can't be negative; labels.length must be >= 0.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.179092180Z"}
{"id":"f786e2cc-1939-4a35-b197-43e5b1d94ec5","expr":"keys != null && labels != null","rationale":"The keys and labels arrays are required and assumed non-null to support iteration and processing.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.199953657Z"}
{"id":"58bd0251-30bc-47a8-8be9-cbc9996163be","expr":"keys.length == labels.length","rationale":"The keys and labels arrays represent a mapping from keys to labels; they must be of equal length.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.199953657Z"}
{"id":"73679adb-2ff9-4f68-92d4-d2e759f984b8","expr":"dflt != null","rationale":"The default label is needed for the switch instruction and should not be null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.199953657Z"}
{"id":"54ace5a3-0950-4418-8404-8450e84c6bca","expr":"labels.length >= 0","rationale":"Array lengths are non-negative by definition.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.199953657Z"}
{"id":"d5f7731e-7972-4d9d-902f-cf085f6f2dbe","expr":"keys.length >= 0","rationale":"Array lengths are non-negative by definition.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.199953657Z"}
{"id":"dd8f9b11-6562-4e32-96a3-565173165d2f","expr":"dflt != null","rationale":"The default label must be provided and is used immediately.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitSwitchInsn(Label,Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.203315626Z"}
{"id":"01d3cd6e-d580-45f7-afc1-668246f2c700","expr":"labels != null","rationale":"The labels array must be provided to add successors.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitSwitchInsn(Label,Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.203315626Z"}
{"id":"c2e081dc-a09f-412f-af09-32ba87e7f21a","expr":"labels.length >= 0","rationale":"Labels is an array, so length is non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitSwitchInsn(Label,Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.203315626Z"}
{"id":"1a8197db-f925-45fb-a683-34f715d3c430","expr":"dflt.getCanonicalInstance() != null","rationale":"The method calls getCanonicalInstance on dflt and expects it non-null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitSwitchInsn(Label,Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.203315626Z"}
