{"id":"54349ffd-3363-4f4a-b5d1-1b5170ad4429","expr":"result != null","rationale":"The method returns an AnnotationWriter created from AnnotationWriter.create, which never returns null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInsnAnnotation(int,TypePath,String,boolean):AnnotationVisitor","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.265782865Z"}
{"id":"78ace7a6-d2ba-40a2-be3e-ca6c3f10b83d","expr":"start != null","rationale":"The start Label is used directly in creating a new Handler instance, so it must be non-null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTryCatchBlock(Label,Label,Label,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.267279443Z"}
{"id":"466d8836-7d81-492d-9450-50db58e6a74c","expr":"end != null","rationale":"The end Label is also passed to the Handler constructor, indicating it should be non-null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTryCatchBlock(Label,Label,Label,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.267279443Z"}
{"id":"f9b61a43-3155-4214-8e70-fe71aa0a662c","expr":"handler != null","rationale":"The handler Label is used directly in the Handler constructor and thus must be non-null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTryCatchBlock(Label,Label,Label,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.267279443Z"}
{"id":"555aeb5b-56f2-4ba6-b295-b731448e6059","expr":"(start.position < end.position)","rationale":"In a try-catch block, the start label must precede the end label, so start.position < end.position should hold.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTryCatchBlock(Label,Label,Label,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:44.267279443Z"}
