{"id":"3e4173d8-72ad-48c3-b711-4ccaff449c6a","expr":"type >= 0","rationale":"The 'type' parameter usually corresponds to a frame type constant and should be non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitFrame(int,int,Object[],int,Object[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.802417441Z"}
{"id":"fd9ffb17-50b9-4387-9a97-dcf5ba539231","expr":"numLocal >= 0","rationale":"numLocal is a count of local variables, so it cannot be negative.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitFrame(int,int,Object[],int,Object[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.802417441Z"}
{"id":"bf2e7321-4e81-4b01-951b-77aa9d6b7e9a","expr":"local == null || local.length >= numLocal","rationale":"Local array length must cover the declared number of local variables.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitFrame(int,int,Object[],int,Object[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.802278399Z"}
{"id":"a1ca161a-1322-42c4-aaab-745ae65a3682","expr":"stack == null || stack.length >= numStack","rationale":"Stack array length must cover the declared stack elements.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitFrame(int,int,Object[],int,Object[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.802278399Z"}
{"id":"93f27fde-5670-4a76-8588-fd2446c336fe","expr":"local == null || local.length >= numLocal","rationale":"Either local array is null or it holds at least numLocal elements.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitFrame(int,int,Object[],int,Object[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.802417441Z"}
{"id":"4c9b3e5a-fb13-4ce9-ba1e-b406403acac6","expr":"numStack >= 0","rationale":"numStack is a count of stack elements, so it cannot be negative.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitFrame(int,int,Object[],int,Object[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.802417441Z"}
{"id":"5ae77020-81b1-4099-98e8-a27abb5586f6","expr":"stack == null || stack.length >= numStack","rationale":"Either stack array is null or it holds at least numStack elements.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitFrame(int,int,Object[],int,Object[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.802417441Z"}
{"id":"0eec2ad4-ebe5-43a9-bf0e-0066634af0a0","expr":"opcode >= 0","rationale":"Opcodes generally correspond to a set of predefined instruction constants which are non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitInsn(int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.809082890Z"}
{"id":"23c9389e-85d2-4958-a4da-f3e49c01b689","expr":"opcode <= 255","rationale":"Opcodes in JVM bytecode are usually defined as single byte values.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitInsn(int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.809082890Z"}
{"id":"4d86b78f-4294-49b9-8a12-c2f380794f3f","expr":"!((opcode >= 0) && (opcode < 0))","rationale":"Trivial sanity check to reflect validity of opcode bounds.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitInsn(int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.809082890Z"}
{"id":"cd5e9fdc-e0db-4479-ac77-486b9ceb3493","expr":"opcode != -1","rationale":"Ensures opcode is not an invalid or special error code value.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitInsn(int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.809082890Z"}
{"id":"2c33d63a-e6ea-4d68-9f1f-a6292fa0c111","expr":"opcode >= 0","rationale":"Opcode should represent a valid instruction code and is non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitInsn(int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.809519192Z"}
{"id":"84743c6e-5fa5-4adc-899c-a66b430d260a","expr":"opcode <= 255","rationale":"Opcode fits in a byte as opcodes in ASM range from 0 to 255.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitInsn(int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.809519192Z"}
{"id":"ef25a503-4cac-4cc7-b05f-732a3af790c1","expr":"opcode >= 0 && opcode <= 255","rationale":"The opcode parameter generally represents a byte opcode value within the 0 to 255 range.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitIntInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.809606456Z"}
{"id":"8d436cbb-d1aa-473a-9277-f1f479fc826a","expr":"(opcode == 16) || (opcode == 17) || (opcode == 188)","rationale":"Based on ASM's IntInsn opcodes, opcode should be among valid int instruction opcodes.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitIntInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.809606456Z"}
{"id":"a30dbe09-4967-423f-b6e7-f337e816b646","expr":"operand >= 0","rationale":"Operands for int instructions like BIPUSH, SIPUSH, and NEWARRAY are non-negative integers.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitIntInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.809606456Z"}
{"id":"60b4e6d6-1207-4171-ae88-cb4ca27244fc","expr":"(opcode != 188) || (operand >= 4 && operand <= 11)","rationale":"When opcode is NEWARRAY, operand specifies array type code within specific range.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitIntInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.809606456Z"}
