{"id":"b52fa652-04df-490b-8544-352189f32200","expr":"label != null","rationale":"The method uses the label parameter directly, so it must be non-null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLabel(Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.829824601Z"}
{"id":"9dee817f-9724-45be-a651-fc4817e5e8f6","expr":"label != null","rationale":"The method processes a label that it expects to be non-null to function properly.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLabel(Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.830443126Z"}
{"id":"2e760b23-ff22-46a0-83fa-027f788b09d7","expr":"label.info == null || label.position >= 0","rationale":"If label.info is null, the label has probably not yet been assigned a position; else, the position should be non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLabel(Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.830443126Z"}
{"id":"2c891adf-39ea-4b93-9071-0b93b7c89dc6","expr":"label.sourcePosition >= 0 || label.info == null","rationale":"Labels with info generally have a valid source position.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLabel(Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.830443126Z"}
{"id":"3801628d-71b5-430c-834b-81e5fa50b628","expr":"label.frame == null || label.frame.owner == label","rationale":"If the label manages frames, those frames should correctly reference their parent label.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLabel(Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.830443126Z"}
{"id":"15678bbe-0f17-462d-939c-723a06931e85","expr":"label.successors == null || label.successors.length >= 0","rationale":"If the label has successors, the array length must be non-negative since length is never negative in Java arrays.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLabel(Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.830443126Z"}
{"id":"7a77bdf9-a55a-4564-b305-86a05e03095d","expr":"value != null || value == null","rationale":"Value can be any object or null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLdcInsn(Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.831233254Z"}
{"id":"aa428601-31d7-4603-9201-0d4ee22e229c","expr":"varIndex >= 0","rationale":"Local variables in bytecode are indexed from zero upwards, so varIndex should be non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.832381295Z"}
{"id":"d6f9394b-6bea-4213-8fed-517d02bdc68f","expr":"increment != 0","rationale":"IINC with a zero increment means no change, so increment is expected to be non-zero.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.832381295Z"}
{"id":"8c9ea1a7-9493-414d-970f-1e94ced811ce","expr":"increment >= Byte.MIN_VALUE && increment <= Byte.MAX_VALUE","rationale":"In JVM bytecode, the increment is a signed byte between -128 and 127.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.832381295Z"}
{"id":"beeb41fd-5a0a-4114-92d3-7091eb113090","expr":"max >= min","rationale":"The max value should be greater or equal to the min value for a valid table switch range.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.838298095Z"}
{"id":"8c6f7282-b194-4d7f-a1eb-4290501533a4","expr":"labels != null","rationale":"The labels array must be non-null as it contains the jump targets.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.838298095Z"}
{"id":"cd1dc619-d6c1-41f9-b0a6-234e46fa70c4","expr":"labels.length >= (max - min + 1)","rationale":"The number of labels should at least cover the range from min to max inclusive.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.838298095Z"}
{"id":"53ec24a8-4b9d-4561-81ee-ab938325564c","expr":"dflt != null","rationale":"The default label must be non-null as the default jump target.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.838298095Z"}
{"id":"2578e81c-9295-442e-83f2-69dc522f7e77","expr":"value != null","rationale":"In general usage, value passed to visitLdcInsn is expected to be non-null as null constants are not handled as operands.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLdcInsn(Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.835100194Z"}
{"id":"7aab1a17-6331-43cc-acca-8e77341c8e3c","expr":"max >= min","rationale":"The table switch bounds must maintain max greater or equal to min to represent a valid range.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.839438872Z"}
{"id":"60c978e0-77de-4404-814b-3bc78131ae72","expr":"labels.length == max - min + 1","rationale":"The labels array length should be exactly max - min + 1 for the table switch mapping.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.839438872Z"}
{"id":"4414b448-ff2f-4a9e-81a0-3a33f27b25c9","expr":"dflt != null","rationale":"The default label for the table switch must not be null as it is the fallback branch.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.839438872Z"}
{"id":"691b1a6a-472f-4e22-b0ac-b142529e0ec3","expr":"labels != null","rationale":"The labels array must be non-null because it provides the jump targets for the switch.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.839438872Z"}
{"id":"decab353-da03-4913-a5a6-539e53ce8bf3","expr":"min <= max + 1","rationale":"To allow for valid or empty ranges, min is allowed to be at most max + 1.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.839438872Z"}
{"id":"8257a7bc-e078-4eca-b294-d635d8ded530","expr":"varIndex >= 0","rationale":"In JVM bytecode, variable indexes used in instructions like IINC are non-negative integers.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.833592435Z"}
{"id":"943386d7-ed9f-47b0-8ee2-21789bd3b522","expr":"increment != 0","rationale":"The IINC instruction increments a local variable by a non-zero amount to have effect.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.833592435Z"}
{"id":"9d9e0086-a1ac-472d-848a-34e0ca97fa24","expr":"Math.abs(increment) <= 127","rationale":"The JVM specification limits the increment operand in IINC instruction to a signed 8-bit value.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.833592435Z"}
{"id":"1745a948-6877-4672-ab99-0725a3c0ca7a","expr":"varIndex <= 65535","rationale":"In JVM bytecode, the variable index is generally limited to 16-bit unsigned values.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.833592435Z"}
{"id":"2be72d60-6973-4c39-b809-c83ba44f1371","expr":"keys != null","rationale":"The keys array is essential for the lookup switch to have values to match keys against.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.839536877Z"}
{"id":"6b986520-1511-4dac-b222-d9e41a4b5c53","expr":"labels != null","rationale":"Labels provide jump targets for the matching keys.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.839536877Z"}
{"id":"634577d8-01ab-4f7f-b866-8b833ed61443","expr":"labels.length == keys.length","rationale":"The keys and labels arrays are matched pairwise by index.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.839536877Z"}
{"id":"c802d980-3c3e-41d5-8a21-848f1769df82","expr":"dflt != null","rationale":"The default label is the fall-through target.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.839536877Z"}
{"id":"3e09f7b2-4733-477e-ba4f-af694d9c7037","expr":"keys.length >= 0","rationale":"Safety invariant about array length.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.839536877Z"}
{"id":"d240bdb2-4603-4802-bf21-4bb0f130648e","expr":"keys == null || labels != null","rationale":"In JVM bytecode, the number of keys and labels correspond to switch cases, so labels should not be null if keys exist.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.840530798Z"}
{"id":"ece08a32-579d-421f-ad00-f18ec551504b","expr":"keys == null || labels.length == keys.length","rationale":"Each key corresponds to one label in the lookup switch, so their lengths must be equal.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.840530798Z"}
{"id":"4ad1daf7-2187-4dd6-9b40-4a7a98889fa8","expr":"dflt != null","rationale":"A lookup switch requires a default label to jump to when keys don't match.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.840530798Z"}
{"id":"9969c948-8b0e-4da9-ad16-ac6fd36beb30","expr":"keys == null || keys.length > 0","rationale":"It is not meaningful to have an empty keys array for the lookup switch; if present, keys array has positive length.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.840530798Z"}
{"id":"66a6c383-f4b5-4324-ae15-63f69307aa30","expr":"labels == null || labels.length > 0","rationale":"Labels array corresponds to switch cases and should have positive length if not null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.840530798Z"}
{"id":"11e61b8f-d5ea-406e-b6c2-299ad272d549","expr":"descriptor != null","rationale":"The method is expected to handle a non-null descriptor string specifying the array type.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitMultiANewArrayInsn(String,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.848473362Z"}
{"id":"ca7d633d-3ce9-4923-8ca6-a1f5329e1662","expr":"numDimensions > 0","rationale":"numDimensions represents the array dimensions and must be at least 1 to define a valid multi-dimensional array.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitMultiANewArrayInsn(String,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.848473362Z"}
{"id":"61267fe8-3787-4fb8-897f-be857821764f","expr":"numDimensions <= descriptor.length()","rationale":"The descriptor must encode the array type such that the number of dimensions does not exceed the descriptor length.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitMultiANewArrayInsn(String,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.848473362Z"}
{"id":"eae62e0d-d789-427a-9b6a-981476371e6c","expr":"descriptor != null","rationale":"The descriptor parameter is typically a non-null string describing the annotation.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitInsnAnnotation(int,TypePath,String,boolean):AnnotationVisitor","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.848795468Z"}
{"id":"986c5eb4-56d7-4664-8550-108217808212","expr":"typePath == null || typePath.getLength() >= 0","rationale":"If typePath is present, its length is non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitInsnAnnotation(int,TypePath,String,boolean):AnnotationVisitor","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.848795468Z"}
{"id":"1f4e2fad-329e-41f3-b04e-9e6b85551fc4","expr":"visible == true || visible == false","rationale":"visible is a boolean parameter, so it can only be true or false.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitInsnAnnotation(int,TypePath,String,boolean):AnnotationVisitor","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.848795468Z"}
{"id":"89cc45df-2dcc-4fc2-8c9e-120d6ee11657","expr":"typeRef >= 0","rationale":"typeRef typically encodes a reference and is non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitInsnAnnotation(int,TypePath,String,boolean):AnnotationVisitor","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.848795468Z"}
{"id":"d5cf6668-8e5a-410f-83d7-88b190e96413","expr":"descriptor.startsWith(\"[\")","rationale":"The descriptor for a multi-dimensional array starts with one or more '[' characters, one per dimension.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitMultiANewArrayInsn(String,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.848473362Z"}
{"id":"5e4389c2-d310-48e9-854d-e885643c2c75","expr":"descriptor.length() >= numDimensions + 1","rationale":"The descriptor has a prefix for every dimension plus a character for the base type; thus length should be at least numDimensions + 1.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitMultiANewArrayInsn(String,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.848473362Z"}
{"id":"8e991f23-6c8f-451a-8a37-ddd5b0738e14","expr":"start != null","rationale":"The start label marks the beginning of the try block and must exist.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTryCatchBlock(Label,Label,Label,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.849394837Z"}
{"id":"bdcd0815-0e29-409d-a34b-5d1bafab4f85","expr":"end != null","rationale":"The end label marks the end of the try block and must exist.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTryCatchBlock(Label,Label,Label,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.849394837Z"}
{"id":"776cfd57-bc4a-48c5-816c-684a1634c534","expr":"handler != null","rationale":"The exception handler label must be present to catch exceptions.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTryCatchBlock(Label,Label,Label,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.849394837Z"}
{"id":"748b350d-ca6c-4468-add0-fa9216aa2c38","expr":"start.getOffset() <= end.getOffset()","rationale":"The start label must not be positioned after the end of the try block.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTryCatchBlock(Label,Label,Label,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.849394837Z"}
{"id":"87468041-f078-47b7-8367-bde1b0d3cb36","expr":"(type == null) || (!type.isEmpty())","rationale":"If type is non-null, it typically identifies the exception class and should not be empty.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTryCatchBlock(Label,Label,Label,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.849394837Z"}
{"id":"2717288d-51a9-403e-a5d8-676fa7f3ad9b","expr":"start != null","rationale":"start label for try block should be non-null since it's mandatory to define the start of try range.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTryCatchBlock(Label,Label,Label,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.850166921Z"}
{"id":"60b54913-9c25-4dff-9624-4279e8ce590a","expr":"!visible || result != null","rationale":"A visible annotation should yield a non-null visitor.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTryCatchAnnotation(int,TypePath,String,boolean):AnnotationVisitor","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.850293429Z"}
{"id":"386d49a6-3ad0-4095-a83b-ac2c138fe28b","expr":"descriptor != null","rationale":"The descriptor should be a valid descriptor string indicating the annotation type.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTryCatchAnnotation(int,TypePath,String,boolean):AnnotationVisitor","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.850209681Z"}
{"id":"55a72f7b-4a73-401c-aaf4-f44022e8f6be","expr":"typePath == null || typePath.isEmpty() == false","rationale":"If typePath is provided, it typically represents a non-empty path; otherwise, it can be null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTryCatchAnnotation(int,TypePath,String,boolean):AnnotationVisitor","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.850209681Z"}
{"id":"c8967041-0c92-42fd-86d6-6d9e49b1291d","expr":"typeRef >= 0","rationale":"Type references in ASM are usually non-negative integers representing bytecode elements.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTryCatchAnnotation(int,TypePath,String,boolean):AnnotationVisitor","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.850209681Z"}
{"id":"6a2af671-7c58-4db5-9e7e-3725d38bbaba","expr":"visible == true || visible == false","rationale":"The visible parameter indicates the visibility of the annotation and must be boolean; this expression is tautological but acceptable for completeness.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTryCatchAnnotation(int,TypePath,String,boolean):AnnotationVisitor","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.850209681Z"}
{"id":"5e9e032e-67ea-4ea7-a114-71c3ef405177","expr":"typeRef <= 0xFFFFFFF","rationale":"Ensures that typeRef fits within the expected bit pattern used for type references in ASM.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTryCatchAnnotation(int,TypePath,String,boolean):AnnotationVisitor","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.850209681Z"}
{"id":"d1f49d29-3051-4b7c-9b80-a55747f6ba19","expr":"end != null","rationale":"end label for try block should be non-null as the range needs an end.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTryCatchBlock(Label,Label,Label,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.850166921Z"}
{"id":"2ead4574-3566-4a5b-a82b-4571c78bd1af","expr":"handler != null","rationale":"handler label must be non-null since it defines the start of the catch block.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTryCatchBlock(Label,Label,Label,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.850166921Z"}
{"id":"160721b4-0865-4348-bfdc-a21db2d07bc5","expr":"!start.equals(end)","rationale":"The try block's start and end labels should differ, defining a non-empty instruction range.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTryCatchBlock(Label,Label,Label,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.850166921Z"}
{"id":"605f5620-9cbc-4731-9262-1b4fd9194f74","expr":"type == null || type.length() > 0","rationale":"The type is either null (catching all exceptions) or a non-empty fully qualified class name.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitTryCatchBlock(Label,Label,Label,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.850166921Z"}
{"id":"76ddd68d-373c-4c05-b0f6-b08e1b2ddd2f","expr":"name != null","rationale":"Name of the variable should be non-null for identification.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodVisitor#visitLocalVariable(String,String,String,Label,Label,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodVisitor.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T14:17:47.850669597Z"}
